WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:05.920
Well, localization is a remarkable phenomenon,
in which the propagation of waves can be confined

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:12.230
in a very small portion of their original
domain although nothing visibly prevents it.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:19.420
One can imagine, for example, a drum in which
vibrations stay in a tiny portion of the membrane

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.890
— for no apparent reason.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.660
But one talks about the localization of waves
more generally.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.090
One shouldn't imagine purely mechanical vibrations.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.480
Light is waves, and sound propagation is waves.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.400
And, from the point of view of quantum physics,
even matter is waves.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:45.260
Localization can be caused by irregularities
of the boundaries, by impurities of the material,

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.590
or by some sort of disorder.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:53.270
And then particularly, a very well known example
of localization is Anderson localization by

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:57.820
disorder for quantum states of electrons.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:02.880
The problem with localization is that there
is a great variety of waves, and there is

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.510
an infinite number of even simplest blocks
of waves which we call eigenfunctions.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:13.390
So it is very difficult to understand and
describe all of them at the same time.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:18.180
The landscape function is sort of a magic
information box — a solution to one simple

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:24.799
mathematical equation — which tells us where
eigenfunctions are localized, where the waves

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:31.170
are localized, what are their shapes and it
even tells us what are the energies at which

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.390
localization occurs.

